From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: window previews on the shelf

Window previews on the shelf are on: hovering an app's shelf button shows
a live preview of its window, and in the menu a click opens for an app
with several windows, the highlighted window's preview shows beside the
list of their titles. Dresden, 2026-11-09: "hovering over chromium or
firefox or whatever app you have open gives no preview. Should be more
like KDE with its window previews".

ChromeOS has the code (ash/shelf/shelf_window_preview_bubble.cc, new in
2026: a mirror of the window, as Overview's) behind kWindowPreviewOnShelf,
off by default. Tried on a test PC with the feature turned on by hand:
the menu's previews show for the browser's windows.

diff --git a/ash/constants/ash_features.cc b/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
index 280a031..2d46212 100644
--- a/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
+++ b/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
@@ -1812,7 +1812,8 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kWifiSyncUploadProxyConfigs, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kWifiSyncApplyProxyConfigs, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Enables window preview on hover for shelf app icons and menu items.
-BASE_FEATURE(kWindowPreviewOnShelf, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// NickelOS: on (Dresden 2026-11-09: window previews as on KDE).
+BASE_FEATURE(kWindowPreviewOnShelf, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Enables an experimental feature that splits windows by dragging one window
 // over another window.
